# The slot premise: each top-level user of the slot gets a token as the
# slot's last user left it.
TlsSlot::entry	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# Inline assembly checked with Isla (verus/ISLA.md): run.sh checks the
# memory each reads or writes and the registers it writes against the
# contract verus/isla/seams.md quotes; what the slot holds rests on the
# loader and the slot premise above.
get	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: on aarch64, that the code is at a user address; on x86_64, that the code is at a user address, and that the task runs in 64-bit mode with linear addresses the memory's (the runs' function assumption and application view); and that the loader maps the GOT entry, 8-byte aligned, at a user address and fills it with the slot's TLS offset, that the slot (the thread pointer plus that offset) is an 8-byte aligned user address, and that the slot holds the cell's value)
get_tp	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: on aarch64, that the code is at a user address; and that the loader maps the GOT entry, 8-byte aligned, at a user address and fills it with the slot's TLS offset, that the slot (the thread pointer plus that offset) is an 8-byte aligned user address, that the slot holds the cell's value, and that TPIDR_EL0 holds the cell's tp)
set	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	trusted (partly checked, Isla: verus/isla/seams.md; not checked: on aarch64, that the code is at a user address; on x86_64, that the code is at a user address, and that the task runs in 64-bit mode with linear addresses the memory's (the runs' function assumption and application view); and that the loader maps the GOT entry, 8-byte aligned, at a user address and fills it with the slot's TLS offset, that the slot (the thread pointer plus that offset) is an 8-byte aligned user address, and that only these sequences touch the slot)
